    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d805">

                <pb facs="0817" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg705"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5117: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commissioner at Helsingfors</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Haynes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Helsingfors</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-27T11:00:00+01:39"><hi rendition="#italic">August 27,
                                1919, 11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:30
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>389. Northern Russian Army Corps after receiving its new supply of English tanks
                    has been driven back and Pskov captured by Bolsheviks, the probable result being
                    that Esthonia may make peace with Soviet or be driven into Bolshevikism by the
                    harassing of Gough<anchor n="43" xml:id="d805-f1"/> and Judenitch.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Haynes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d805-f1" n="43" xml:id="d805-f1-content">
                <p>Lt. Gen. Sir Hubert Gough, chief of the British mission to the Baltic States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
